  repos/npm is an on-demand cache rather than a bulk index, so it grows when a
  run asks for a name it lacks; eval/npm/seed.sh and a FILL=1 scale.sh run
  deliberately fill a symlink farm under the run directory instead, leaving
  this tree untouched, and the measured sweeps then run against a frozen
  shim.  A changed hash here means something wrote into the checkout.

  All of it was fetched from registry.npmjs.org on 2026-09-24 between 12:46
  and 12:53 UTC, not by scripts/fetch-repos.sh.  The 3992 names
  eval/npm/names.txt lists, which are the queries of a scale run, were fetched
  first.  The other 1236 packuments are what closing the snapshot over both
  sides' cones fetched: 50 by seed.sh's --fill, which also chose
  baseline/roots.txt, and 1186 by a FILL=1 scale.sh pass over every query,
  copied here from the farms unchanged -- pac reads them as well, through
  --cache, so without them the sweep reproduces only from one machine's
  scratch directory.  tarballs/ holds the three tarballs npm opens because the
  version bundles its dependencies (npm 11.20.0 and 12.1.0, request 2.11.4);
  setup.sh links them beside the farm, where the shim serves them.  A frozen
  scale.sh run over every query then asked for nothing this tree lacks except
  one git repository (esprima#harmony, which recast 0.5.27 names), which no
  snapshot of the registry holds.

The cargo sweeps need nothing pinned beyond repos/crates.io-index above: both
of them ask cargo only for a lockfile, which it resolves from index rows alone
and writes without downloading a single crate body.  There is no CARGO_HOME
cache in the universe they answer about, and so none to record here.
